# cc-leash reads no secrets. Every variable below is optional; the defaults
# are shown. Export them in your shell (cc-leash does not load .env files).
# Never put payment API keys in your shell: see SECURITY.md ("The curl bypass").

# Claude Code's config directory. leash keeps its policy and ledger under it.
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude

# Directory for the ledger.
# LEASH_HOME=$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/leash

# Ledger file path (overrides LEASH_HOME for the ledger).
# LEASH_LEDGER=$LEASH_HOME/ledger.jsonl

# Global policy file.
# LEASH_GLOBAL_CONFIG=$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/leash.json

# Project root where .leash.json is read. Claude Code sets this for hooks;
# set it yourself only when running the CLI outside the project directory.
# CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=

# examples/demo/demo.sh: working directory for the demo session and its
# throwaway ledger. Default: a new temp directory.
# LEASH_DEMO_DIR=

# examples/fakepay/server.mjs: if set, each fake payment is appended here as JSONL.
# FAKEPAY_LOG=
